{"content":[{"c":["ISHI"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Appaim’s son, the father of Sheshan and a descendant of Judah through Jerahmeel’s line (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.2.31","r":"1Chr.2.31","rawR":"1Chr.2.31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.2.31","value":"1Chr.2.31"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 2:31"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Man from Judah’s tribe whose descendants were Zoheth and Ben-zoheth (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.4.20","r":"1Chr.4.20","rawR":"1Chr.4.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.4.20","value":"1Chr.4.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 4:20"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Simeonite whose four sons led 500 men to Mt Seir, where they destroyed the remnant Amalekites and settled their own people (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.4.42","r":"1Chr.4.42","rawR":"1Chr.4.42","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.4.42","value":"1Chr.4.42"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 4:42"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["4. One of the leaders of the half-tribe of Manasseh east of the Jordan (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.5.24","r":"1Chr.5.24","rawR":"1Chr.5.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.5.24","value":"1Chr.5.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 5:24"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["5. Name of God, meaning “my husband,” by which Israel will one day address him (",{"href":"?bref=Hos.2.16","r":"Hos.2.16","rawR":"Hos.2.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Hos.2.16","value":"Hos.2.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Hos 2:16"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=GodNamesof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"GodNamesof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"GodNamesof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"God, Names of"},"."],"sourceClass":"list-text","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Ishi","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Chr 2:31","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_map